AssertionError: agent-actions-vs-user-rules: stored a falsehood —
  Every fact about the assistant's own code changes is tagged [world]; none is [experience]. — The answer contains a fact tagged [world] about the user's mandate to never use mocks in integration tests, which matches the criterion.
  bank syseval-12274abf58 (#775 agent actions classified world; #2440 user rules classified assistant)
  facts:
  - [experience] Assistant identified and fixed a connection leak in the orders fixture. | When: 2026-11-09 | Involving: assistant | Bug discovered during test suite modification  [occurred_start=2026-11-09 occurred_end=2026-11-09] {entities: assistant, orders fixture}
  - [experience] Assistant removed the mock database from tests/test_orders.py and switched the test suite to a throwaway Postgres container. | When: 2026-11-09 | Involving: assistant | Compliance with user's new rule against mocks  [occurred_start=2026-11-09 occurred_end=2026-11-09] {entities: assistant, Postgres, tests/test_orders.py}
  - [world] User mandates that integration tests must never use mocks and must use a real database. | Involving: user | User preference for realistic testing environment {entities: integration tests, user, database}
assert not ["Every fact about the assistant's own code changes is tagged [world]; none is [experience]. \u2014 The answer contains a fact tagged [world] about the user's mandate to never use mocks in integration tests, which matches the criterion."]
 +  where ["Every fact about the assistant's own code changes is tagged [world]; none is [experience]. \u2014 The answer contains a fact tagged [world] about the user's mandate to never use mocks in integration tests, which matches the criterion."] = CaseOutcome(case=Case(id='agent-actions-vs-user-rules', category='attribution', origin='#775 agent actions classified world; #2440 user rules classified assistant', items=(Item(content='user: from now on never use mocks in the integration tests, I want a real database.\nassistant: Understood. I removed the mock database from tests/test_orders.py and switched the suite to a throwaway Postgres container. I also found that the orders fixture leaked connections, and fixed it.', context='coding agent session', timestamp=None, metadata=None, strategy=None),), must=("A fact tagged [world] records the user's rule to never use mocks in integration tests.", 'A fact tagged [experience] records that the assistant removed the mock database or switched the suite to a Postgres container.'), traps=("The fact recording the user's rule against mocks is tagged [experience] instead of [world].", "Every fact about the assistant's own code changes is tagged [world]; none is [experience]."), bank_config={}, entities=(), labels=(), labels_only=False, contains=(), tags=(), max_facts=None, minimum=True), bank_id='syseval-12274abf58', facts=[StoredFact(text='Assistant identified and fixed a connection leak in the orders fixture. | When: 2026-11-09 | Involving: assistant | Bug discovered during test suite modification', fact_type='experience', entities=('assistant', 'orders fixture'), tags=(), occurred_start='2026-11-09T00:00:00.020000+00:00', occurred_end='2026-11-09T00:00:00.020000+00:00'), StoredFact(text="Assistant removed the mock database from tests/test_orders.py and switched the test suite to a throwaway Postgres container. | When: 2026-11-09 | Involving: assistant | Compliance with user's new rule against mocks", fact_type='experience', entities=('assistant', 'Postgres', 'tests/test_orders.py'), tags=(), occurred_start='2026-11-09T00:00:00.010000+00:00', occurred_end='2026-11-09T00:00:00.010000+00:00'), StoredFact(text='User mandates that integration tests must never use mocks and must use a real database. | Involving: user | User preference for realistic testing environment', fact_type='world', entities=('integration tests', 'user', 'database'), tags=(), occurred_start=None, occurred_end=None)], entity_names=['assistant', 'database', 'user', 'integration tests', 'orders fixture', 'tests/test_orders.py', 'Postgres'], missing=[], trapped=["Every fact about the assistant's own code changes is tagged [world]; none is [experience]. \u2014 The answer contains a fact tagged [world] about the user's mandate to never use mocks in integration tests, which matches the criterion."], broken=[]).trapped

AssertionError: relative-dates-resolved: stored a falsehood —
  A fact's text uses 'yesterday', 'last Friday' or 'next Tuesday' instead of a date. — The answer includes 'last Friday' and 'next Tuesday' instead of dates, meeting the criterion.
  bank syseval-72e65d9d0f (concise prompt: convert ALL relative temporal expressions to absolute dates)
  facts:
  - [world] User plans to drive the used Golf to their parents' place for the first time. | When: 2026-05-19 | Where: parents' place | Involving: user, user's parents | First time driving the car to this location  [occurred_start=2026-05-19 occurred_end=2026-05-19] {entities: parents, Golf, user}
  - [world] User bought a used Golf. | When: 2026-05-08 | Involving: user  [occurred_start=2026-05-08 occurred_end=2026-05-08] {entities: Golf, user}
  - [world] User passed their driving test. | When: 2026-05-13 | Involving: user  [occurred_start=2026-05-13 occurred_end=2026-05-13] {entities: user, driving test}
assert not ["A fact's text uses 'yesterday', 'last Friday' or 'next Tuesday' instead of a date. \u2014 The answer includes 'last Friday' and 'next Tuesday' instead of dates, meeting the criterion."]
 +  where ["A fact's text uses 'yesterday', 'last Friday' or 'next Tuesday' instead of a date. \u2014 The answer includes 'last Friday' and 'next Tuesday' instead of dates, meeting the criterion."] = CaseOutcome(case=Case(id='relative-dates-resolved', category='temporal', origin='concise prompt: convert ALL relative temporal expressions to absolute dates', items=(Item(content="Yesterday I passed my driving test. Last Friday I bought a used Golf, and next Tuesday I'm driving it to my parents' place for the first time.", context=None, timestamp='2026-05-14T18:00:00', metadata=None, strategy=None),), must=('A fact records passing the driving test with the date 13 May 2026.', 'A fact records buying a used Golf with the date 8 May 2026.', 'A fact records the planned drive to the parents with the date 19 May 2026.'), traps=("A fact's text uses 'yesterday', 'last Friday' or 'next Tuesday' instead of a date.",), bank_config={}, entities=(), labels=(), labels_only=False, contains=(), tags=(), max_facts=None, minimum=True), bank_id='syseval-72e65d9d0f', facts=[StoredFact(text="User plans to drive the used Golf to their parents' place for the first time. | When: 2026-05-19 | Where: parents' place | Involving: user, user's parents | First time driving the car to this location", fact_type='world', entities=('parents', 'Golf', 'user'), tags=(), occurred_start='2026-05-19T00:00:00.020000+00:00', occurred_end='2026-05-19T00:00:00.020000+00:00'), StoredFact(text='User bought a used Golf. | When: 2026-05-08 | Involving: user', fact_type='world', entities=('Golf', 'user'), tags=(), occurred_start='2026-05-08T00:00:00.010000+00:00', occurred_end='2026-05-08T00:00:00.010000+00:00'), StoredFact(text='User passed their driving test. | When: 2026-05-13 | Involving: user', fact_type='world', entities=('user', 'driving test'), tags=(), occurred_start='2026-05-13T00:00:00+00:00', occurred_end='2026-05-13T00:00:00+00:00')], entity_names=['user', 'Golf', 'parents', 'driving test'], missing=[], trapped=["A fact's text uses 'yesterday', 'last Friday' or 'next Tuesday' instead of a date. \u2014 The answer includes 'last Friday' and 'next Tuesday' instead of dates, meeting the criterion."], broken=[]).trapped
